title: Microsoft login served by a reverse proxy (AiTM)
severity: critical
score: 80
tags: phishing, aitm
attack: T1557, T1539, T1566.002
description: A non-Microsoft host serves Microsoft login endpoints (oauth2/authorize,
  GetCredentialType, kmsi) with ESTS markers or ESTS cookies. This is an AiTM reverse
  proxy.
---
requests
| where isnotempty(host)
    and not owned_by(host, "Microsoft")
    and host !in list("microsoft.auth_hosts")
    and not allowlisted(host)
| where path matches list("microsoft.auth_path")
// Microsoft's sign-in markup or ESTS session cookies coming back from that host:
// it is relaying Microsoft's real sign-in (an AiTM reverse proxy).
| where resp_text matches list("microsoft.login_page_markers")
    or set_has_any(cookies_set, list("microsoft.ests_cookies"))
| project host, path
